1
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:14,680
When they hit you, you take it.
When they tell you to kneel, you kneel.

2
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:17,433
The weak get crushed by the strong.
That's just how the world works.

3
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:18,518
15 YEARS EARLIER, BUSAN

4
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:22,146
Come here!
Why'd you bring this thing?

5
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:25,858
What? Were you gonna
put a bullet in my head? Huh?

6
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:29,654
A goddamn Jap like you
should know your place.

7
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:33,241
Your brother's probably off
to report his missing pistol,

8
00:00:33,242 --> 00:00:34,992
but you're the one who stole it!

9
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,958
You see what happens, you bastard?

10
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:44,168
Know your damn place, kid. All right?

11
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:48,257
I'm taking this, by the way.

12
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:50,509
What a little shit.

13
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:55,638
Get the hell off me!

14
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:12,489
My brother always said,

15
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:16,742
"If you don't want to get crushed
by your enemies, crush them first."

16
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:17,911
Where is he?

17
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,293
Give me the gun.

18
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,134
Go home and wait till later.

19
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:18,764
Kitae never asked me
why I killed the guy,

20
00:02:20,057 --> 00:02:22,308
and I never asked
what he did with the body.

21
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:24,061
An unspoken agreement.

22
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:31,609
And that day,
the day I thought it was all over,

23
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:32,986
everything began.

24
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:37,925
This is Baek Kihyun.

25
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:39,428
Is Jang back?

26
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,560
Yes. May I help you with something?

27
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:49,604
He just got his hands
on the slush fund ledger.

28
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:53,150
Stay sharp, find out exactly
what's going on, and report back to me.

29
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,609
720-1879.

30
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,864
If anything happens, you call me.
Understood?

31
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:28,684
If you want
your sister to live

32
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:30,979
and your niece to have a normal childhood,

33
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:34,524
you have to ensure you survive first.

34
00:05:00,175 --> 00:05:01,258
- Sir.
- Yeah.

35
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:02,927
We're ready to move out.

36
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:05,554
If we arrest Cheon Seokjung,
will you question him yourself

37
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,014
or will somebody else do it?

38
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:08,391
Baek Kihyun will be up to it.

39
00:05:09,226 --> 00:05:10,518
Baek Kihyun's pretty green.

40
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,728
Let's give him a chance.

41
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:16,315
Did you request a warrant for Cheon?
Just tell me, and be honest.

42
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:17,317
Yes.

43
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:20,487
- You upset about that?
- What'd you charge him with?

44
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:28,077
I told you, we're taking him down
for his slush fund!

45
00:05:28,078 --> 00:05:30,162
And what about the whole drug ring?

46
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,706
We're shifting the investigation
to go after the slush fund,

47
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:34,459
- not the drugs, Miss Oh.
-  Sir, come on.

48
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,336
Are you sure you want this case
to get political?

49
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:38,921
-  Ugh, this girl.
-  "This girl"?

50
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:41,091
- Don't you dare talk to me like that!
- Colonel Ahn!

51
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:44,010
Just relax, both of you.

52
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,430
Ahn, get moving. Let's go.

53
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:52,310
Sir, we're moving out.

54
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:06,283
When we arrest Cheon Seokjung…

55
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:12,831
If you let those politicians in uniform
pull your strings,

56
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:15,709
they'll stab you in the damn back.

57
00:06:18,587 --> 00:06:21,046
SPECIAL ADVISOR JANG GEONYOUNG

58
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:41,359
Yes?

59
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:44,779
This is Baek Kihyun. Where's my brother?

60
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:47,073
He's with Chief Cheon.

61
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:52,037
All right, Cheon is going to be arrested.
Orders came down.

62
00:06:54,456 --> 00:06:56,124
You really think you can handle that?

63
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,251
Oh, it would be my pleasure.

64
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:03,048
I'll do it, my own way.

65
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:25,570
They've issued
an arrest warrant for Chief Cheon.

66
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:32,994
What is it?

67
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:37,332
The JIH has a warrant.
They'll be coming for you soon, sir.

68
00:07:42,504 --> 00:07:44,214
So they're finally doing it.

69
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,425
They're making a move.

70
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:49,928
Better get going.

71
00:07:56,226 --> 00:07:57,435
Forget it.

72
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:02,315
It won't solve anything if I run.

73
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,529
I need you to take out Hwang
for good, Kitae.

74
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:09,823
That's the only way I survive.

75
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,119
Tell me you understand.

76
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:16,662
Yes, absolutely.

77
00:08:26,798 --> 00:08:30,093
Go to your hotel, take a hot shower,
and get some good rest.

78
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:34,681
My investigators will ensure
you get to the airport safely tomorrow.

79
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:39,436
Let's hope the two of us
never meet in Korea again.

80
00:08:57,871 --> 00:08:59,164
Chief Cheon Seokjung.

81
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:02,500
I'm Jang Geonyoung.
Nice to finally meet you.

82
00:09:04,169 --> 00:09:05,795
I've always wanted to introduce myself.

83
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,839
It's a big honor to have you visit.

84
00:09:08,757 --> 00:09:09,799
So, shall we?

85
00:09:11,009 --> 00:09:12,010
Right this way.

86
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:21,853
Get moving, okay?

87
00:09:25,356 --> 00:09:26,566
Choi Yuji.

88
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,028
You did well.

89
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:53,802
Listen, I want you to handle
the interrogation of Chief Cheon yourself.

90
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:58,431
This is a direct order from Advisor Jang,
so don't disappoint us.

91
00:10:08,191 --> 00:10:11,444
Are you sure
that we should use Colonel Baek for this?

92
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:14,697
- I'm on the fence.
- Uh-huh.

93
00:10:15,824 --> 00:10:17,075
Baek's up to it.

94
00:10:17,826 --> 00:10:19,994
I wanna see what his strategy is.

95
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:26,291
This book documents
a 70 billion won slush fund,

96
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,585
which you moved to Japan.

97
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,880
Choi Yuji, the head of the Ikeda clan,
already testified.

98
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,340
She managed the fund.

99
00:10:35,677 --> 00:10:37,929
What are your ties to the Ikeda family?

100
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:44,435
How about this.
Where did you get the money?

101
00:10:48,398 --> 00:10:49,524
Chief Cheon.

102
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,818
If you continue to remain silent,

103
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:56,030
we'll have no choice
but to consider it an admission of guilt.

104
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:05,832
Do you…

105
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:11,504
really want me to be honest here?

106
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:21,514
Just remember…

107
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:27,145
your brother's not gonna look good.

108
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:33,902
Bit of a minefield, eh?

109
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:42,535
You can pretend, but I know you're lying.

110
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:55,797
Ah, ah.
They can hear me, right?

111
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:57,550
Yeah.

112
00:11:58,426 --> 00:11:59,760
Well, Colonel.

113
00:11:59,761 --> 00:12:01,512
I think that's enough for today.

114
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,681
You must be getting tired.

115
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:44,847
You gotta be kidding me.

116
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:48,893
A literal shithole.

117
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:01,572
How's Cheon doing?

118
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:06,160
He's been keeping his mouth shut,
but he won't be able to hold out.

119
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:10,915
Once he starts talking, it's all over.
You know that, right?

120
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:14,460
No, I'm putting an end to it.
He needs to hold out a little longer.

121
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,004
What's your angle now?

122
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,006
You just keep a close eye on him, okay?

123
00:13:19,007 --> 00:13:21,092
Oh, and, where's Choi Yuji?

124
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,136
She was released. She's at a hotel.

125
00:13:24,137 --> 00:13:26,305
She's going back to Japan
on the first flight tomorrow.

126
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:27,432
Which hotel?

127
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:31,184
You won't be able to get to her.
The place is crawling with armed guards.

128
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:33,061
I said, which hotel?

129
00:13:35,982 --> 00:13:38,025
Tower Hotel, Room 925.

130
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:17,774
Colonel Baek…

131
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:26,741
You heading home yet?

132
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:30,536
I have a few more things to do, sir.

133
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:34,499
Don't push yourself too hard.

134
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,209
See you tomorrow.

135
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:32,348
Director Baek,
you're not allowed to see her.

136
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:29,780
Are you all right?

137
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,328
I'm sorry.

138
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:37,872
It was my only option.

139
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:43,920
I would've done the same thing.

140
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:46,130
Don't apologize, please.

141
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:52,595
What are you going to do now?

142
00:16:54,222 --> 00:16:55,431
I told you already.

143
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:59,185
I have to see it through.
I've come this far.

144
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:08,236
We could go to Japan together,
couldn't we?

145
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,404
We could…

146
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,656
just start over.

147
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:14,783
You know my hands are tied right now.

148
00:17:14,784 --> 00:17:15,785
Kitae.

149
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,538
You might die here.

150
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:26,921
Go wait for me in Japan.

151
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,423
As soon as I take care of this,

152
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,134
we'll start over, okay?

153
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:37,682
I'm pretty sure that's a goodbye,
isn't it?

154
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,597
What we had was nice, wasn't it?

155
00:18:20,891 --> 00:18:22,393
It was pretty good.

156
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,439
It was nice.

157
00:18:30,151 --> 00:18:33,195
We'll be able to… meet again, right?

158
00:18:34,614 --> 00:18:35,865
Yes, we will.

159
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:47,168
I'll see you in Ikaino
for a big bowl of rice soup.

160
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:49,295
Just like old times.

161
00:18:51,881 --> 00:18:53,633
I need you to promise me…

162
00:18:57,011 --> 00:18:58,554
that you'll stay alive.

163
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:03,768
I will, I promise.

164
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:05,686
I'll get to Japan.

165
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:20,951
Please, Kitae…

166
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:25,080
when that day comes, let's do it right.

167
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:26,999
Let's not screw up again.

168
00:19:32,672 --> 00:19:34,131
Love is too special.

169
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:39,637
We won't mess it up.

170
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:42,765
I promise, Yuji.

171
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:55,110
ARMY HEADQUARTERS

172
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:57,654
I'd like to thank all the commanders

173
00:19:57,655 --> 00:19:59,323
for attending this meeting today.

174
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:01,616
Above all,

175
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:04,411
I expect you all to make national security
your number one priority.

176
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,495
CHIEF OF STAFF, R.O.K ARMY

177
00:20:05,496 --> 00:20:08,415
Please commit yourself
to the rule of law and order,

178
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:11,334
and work tirelessly
to regain economic stability.

179
00:20:13,087 --> 00:20:15,214
Oh, shoot, sorry about that.

180
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:17,800
Sorry I'm late. Apologies.

181
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:28,394
Oh, sorry, General.
Uh, keep talking.

182
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:30,479
Some water, sir?

183
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:36,735
Very well. If there are no objections…

184
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:40,029
…I'd like to ask the head
of the JIH a brief question.

185
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,949
You know, before we proceed further.

186
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:44,451
Yes, General Jang?

187
00:20:44,452 --> 00:20:46,411
I hear you've been extremely busy.

188
00:20:48,289 --> 00:20:50,707
Extremely? No, sir. No, I'm just…

189
00:20:50,708 --> 00:20:53,168
I'm just trying to do good work
at the job I've been given.

190
00:20:53,169 --> 00:20:55,003
Is that right?

191
00:20:55,004 --> 00:20:57,256
- Yes.
- Then answer me this.

192
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,425
Did I ever give an order

193
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:04,388
for you to take over as chair
of the vice ministers' council?

194
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:08,433
Uh, with martial law in effect,

195
00:21:08,434 --> 00:21:09,976
there seemed to be a lot of confusion

196
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:12,020
with the jurisdictions
of different ministries,

197
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:14,105
so I thought it'd be good for the JIH to--

198
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:18,401
And how do you explain taking Chief Cheon
into punitive custody without permission?

199
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:22,531
Let me guess, you were
going to report that to us after?

200
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,075
Uh, no, sir, no.

201
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:28,411
You'll recall my reports
on credible suspicions

202
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:30,038
of illicit slush fund transactions--

203
00:21:30,039 --> 00:21:32,291
Who the damn hell are you?

204
00:21:35,169 --> 00:21:37,338
Hwang Daesik, nice to meet you.

205
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,715
-  Sir, Hwang is a good man.
- Do you…

206
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:43,092
He wouldn't go
behind your back deliberately.

207
00:21:43,093 --> 00:21:44,928
Please be lenient with him.

208
00:21:44,929 --> 00:21:48,473
I agree, sir. General Hwang
has a lot on his plate right now.

209
00:21:48,474 --> 00:21:50,559
I'm sure this was
just a well-meaning blunder.

210
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:56,564
Is this the duty of an honest soldier?

211
00:21:56,565 --> 00:22:00,568
No, a good soldier knows their role
and they stick to it with integrity!

212
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:03,279
If you want to sneak around
and play politics with each other,

213
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:06,659
then please do me a favor
and get out of my sight right now!

214
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:17,670
General Jang.

215
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:22,007
My sense of loyalty got the better of me.

216
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:24,802
I'll try to be careful of that.

217
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:27,136
"Loyalty"?

218
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,472
That said,

219
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:31,516
we still intend to carry out

220
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:35,729
a full investigation
into all who have amassed illicit wealth.

221
00:22:42,236 --> 00:22:45,029
ILLEGAL SLUSH FUND EXPOSED
SIGNS POINT TO KCIA INVOLVEMENT

222
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:49,285
"Chief of Staff Cheon Seokjung's
Illegal Slush Fund Scheme Exposed.

223
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:54,455
All Signs Point Directly Toward…
KCIA involvement."

224
00:22:54,456 --> 00:22:56,458
DEPUTY DIRECTOR PYO HAKSU

225
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:59,545
Yeah, pretty punchy headline.

226
00:23:11,891 --> 00:23:12,974
Director Baek!

227
00:23:12,975 --> 00:23:16,102
The Joint Investigation
Headquarters announced this morning…

228
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:19,397
- Hey. What's going on?
- …ledger documenting illegal slush funds

229
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:22,066
allegedly maintained by
the Chief of Staff, Cheon Seokjung.

230
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:24,819
The news is sending shock waves
throughout the country…

231
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,446
Did you know about this?

232
00:23:26,447 --> 00:23:29,574
…records of tens of billions of won
in illicit funds, prompting…

233
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:31,951
Oh, fuck, we're screwed! Goddamn…

234
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,703
…the KCIA. According to reports,

235
00:23:33,704 --> 00:23:35,204
the ledger contains…

236
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:37,040
…detailed records spanning several years,

237
00:23:37,041 --> 00:23:40,251
documenting how the funds
were accumulated and distributed.

238
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:43,504
Chief of Staff Cheon Seokjung
is currently being held for questioning

239
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:45,173
at the Joint Investigation Headquarters,

240
00:23:45,174 --> 00:23:47,759
as government officials
continue to examine

241
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:51,054
how the slush fund was created
and where the money was spent.

242
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:54,098
The Joint Investigation Headquarters
stated that it will make further…

243
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:55,100
Yes?

244
00:24:07,237 --> 00:24:10,658
That bastard Hwang.
He never reported it to us.

245
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:14,494
What he's doing is completely outrageous.

246
00:24:14,495 --> 00:24:17,873
That son of a bitch must really
think I'll just roll over 'cause of this.

247
00:24:19,041 --> 00:24:22,293
Madam Shin,
what's the best course of action?

248
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:24,212
What should I do about that asshole?

249
00:24:24,213 --> 00:24:27,632
Well, he must be very pleased
with himself right now.

250
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:31,971
Sometimes it's good to let a man
enjoy his little victories while he can.

251
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:34,223
Show some restraint.

252
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:37,810
Wouldn't you agree, Director Baek?

253
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:44,233
General, don't worry.
I'll take care of it.

254
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:46,526
A crisis is an opportunity.

255
00:24:46,527 --> 00:24:48,569
You'll take care of what, exactly?

256
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:49,947
General Jang.

257
00:24:51,699 --> 00:24:54,451
Be patient. He knows what he's doing.

258
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:57,663
Baek, be honest.

259
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:01,041
Is it true? Seventy billion?

260
00:25:01,709 --> 00:25:03,960
No, it's absurd.

261
00:25:03,961 --> 00:25:06,922
It's all lies that Hwang cooked up.

262
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:12,511
You're right.

263
00:25:13,012 --> 00:25:16,723
Cheon isn't the kind of man
who'd do something like that.

264
00:25:16,724 --> 00:25:20,936
If there's one thing I know about him,
he'd never mess around with money.

265
00:25:21,645 --> 00:25:23,563
Seokjung and I graduated together.

266
00:25:23,564 --> 00:25:25,441
He was ranked first.

267
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:28,736
And I was ranked second.

268
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:37,160
In any case, I'm happy
to entrust this to you, Director.

269
00:25:37,161 --> 00:25:38,162
Yes, sir, I'm on it.

270
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:57,181
I'll be in touch before long.

271
00:26:10,444 --> 00:26:13,530
Heaven Cloud Pavilion. Do you know it?

272
00:26:14,948 --> 00:26:17,950
Well, it's where Bae Geumji worked.

273
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:19,912
One of those old courtesan houses.

274
00:26:20,537 --> 00:26:23,623
Hwang Daesik is going to be there
to have some drinks.

275
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:28,962
Weren't you planning
to get this over with and kill him?

276
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:32,883
You know about that?

277
00:26:35,177 --> 00:26:39,056
You're probably desperate, aren't you?
You're out of options now.

278
00:26:40,808 --> 00:26:41,892
When will he be there?

279
00:26:45,521 --> 00:26:46,980
You broke a girl's heart.

280
00:26:49,316 --> 00:26:51,902
I saw you in my dream last night,
Director Baek.

281
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:56,656
I remember you were out swimming
in deep blue sea water.

282
00:26:56,657 --> 00:27:00,118
You kept calling out to me,
saying I should join you.

283
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:08,168
Then earlier today, before my prayer,
I did a cleansing ritual and…

284
00:27:09,002 --> 00:27:10,129
what a surprise…

285
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:13,590
I saw your face again.

286
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:16,093
I could see it so clearly.

287
00:27:16,718 --> 00:27:18,095
And guess what?

288
00:27:19,847 --> 00:27:22,390
I could tell you'd broken up with someone.

289
00:27:22,391 --> 00:27:24,059
Your expression was clear.

290
00:27:25,811 --> 00:27:28,229
But there are plenty of women out there.

291
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:31,733
So bury the memories in your heart,
and abandon past regrets.

292
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:37,406
It's all right, Kitae.
Somebody new is waiting.

293
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:39,532
Hmm?

294
00:27:42,870 --> 00:27:45,873
Oh, I'll keep you posted on Hwang Daesik.

295
00:27:53,088 --> 00:27:56,258
HEAVEN CLOUD PAVILION

296
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:18,070
It's at Heaven Cloud Pavilion.

297
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:20,991
I confirmed the reservation
under Colonel Ahn's name, sir.

298
00:28:21,575 --> 00:28:22,826
It's for the 13th?

299
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:25,286
That's right.

300
00:28:25,287 --> 00:28:27,330
Get some men you trust,
make sure they're ready.

301
00:28:27,331 --> 00:28:28,873
Pyo should be left out of this.

302
00:28:28,874 --> 00:28:30,249
Yes, sir. I'm on it.

303
00:28:51,021 --> 00:28:52,605
I did my research.

304
00:28:52,606 --> 00:28:54,231
That guy Jang Geonyoung?

305
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:57,611
I tried digging deep,
and it brought up absolutely nothing.

306
00:28:59,863 --> 00:29:01,239
Nobody's close to the guy.

307
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:05,077
He's like a deserted island. All alone.

308
00:29:15,921 --> 00:29:17,130
Uh, so…

309
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:19,341
Sorry about that.

310
00:29:20,634 --> 00:29:22,427
Anyway, the bottom line is…

311
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:28,099
…there is someone
that might be close enough to him.

312
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:30,102
Oh Yejin, the female prosecutor.

313
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:33,689
Not his younger sister?

314
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:38,068
Well, she still lives alone,
no close friends,

315
00:29:39,653 --> 00:29:41,238
no guitar anymore.

316
00:29:42,489 --> 00:29:44,198
She works at the factory still,

317
00:29:44,199 --> 00:29:46,575
but no matter how I look,
there's nothing we can pin on her.

318
00:29:46,576 --> 00:29:48,120
One thing's clear about Jang, though.

319
00:29:49,413 --> 00:29:51,873
He's spent nine years
waiting for an opportunity.

320
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:55,668
Just to bring you down.

321
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,259
You can go.

322
00:30:16,565 --> 00:30:17,899
Sir, I apologize.

323
00:30:27,242 --> 00:30:30,078
Pyo Haksu. You find anything yet?

324
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:34,166
Nothing that suggests he's been in contact
with the JIH up to this point.

325
00:30:36,168 --> 00:30:37,794
I'll continue to monitor him.

326
00:30:40,797 --> 00:30:42,674
What made you want to see me again?

327
00:30:43,675 --> 00:30:45,634
The two of us
don't exactly have a cordial,

328
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:47,678
coffee-house kind of relationship.

329
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:52,183
I suppose you shouldn't have come, then.

330
00:30:52,184 --> 00:30:53,185
What?

331
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:56,188
Wow, that's bitter.

332
00:30:57,564 --> 00:31:00,150
I'm sure you came
because you got worried, right?

333
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:03,444
Cheon Seokjung's picture
is on the front page,

334
00:31:03,445 --> 00:31:04,654
accusations are flying,

335
00:31:05,572 --> 00:31:07,531
and your brother won't tell you anything.

336
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:09,076
You're completely in the dark.

337
00:31:10,827 --> 00:31:12,079
I know you're anxious.

338
00:31:12,621 --> 00:31:13,704
Hey.

339
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:16,458
Just spit out what you came to say.

340
00:31:17,334 --> 00:31:18,335
All right.

341
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:22,339
Park Changbae.

342
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:24,049
Where is he?

343
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:29,971
We've been looking everywhere
and still have no clue.

344
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:33,600
We don't know if he's dead or alive.

345
00:31:34,351 --> 00:31:36,478
You haven't been able
to reach him either, have you?

346
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:42,692
My bet is your brother made him
so terrified, he fled the country.

347
00:31:45,195 --> 00:31:46,238
Then again,

348
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:49,991
Kang Daeil wound up dead,
he wouldn't want the same fate.

349
00:31:51,326 --> 00:31:54,870
You little shit!
Watch your damn mouth, you bitch.

350
00:31:54,871 --> 00:31:58,416
Did you forget what happens
when you challenge my brother?

351
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:01,878
Oh, of course not.

352
00:32:02,504 --> 00:32:05,507
I'm well aware
of what Director Baek Kitae can do.

353
00:32:06,341 --> 00:32:09,678
And I know exactly
who killed Kang Daeil, too.

354
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:18,478
That's right. It wasn't suicide.

355
00:32:20,981 --> 00:32:22,107
It was him.

356
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:25,610
Your own brother took him out. You get it?

357
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:32,075
Oh, man.

358
00:32:48,842 --> 00:32:51,595
Hi, Minju. It's Uncle Kihyun.
Is your mom around?

359
00:32:54,514 --> 00:32:55,890
Where did she go?

360
00:33:03,148 --> 00:33:05,650
Please make sure
that your mother calls me, all right?

361
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:08,028
Mm-hmm. Mmm.

362
00:33:24,127 --> 00:33:25,962
- I won't be gone long.
- Yes, sir.

363
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:30,884
Anything happen while I was gone?

364
00:33:31,968 --> 00:33:33,594
Uh, Miss Oh.

365
00:33:33,595 --> 00:33:36,556
Mr. Jang. He wants to speak with you.

366
00:33:48,944 --> 00:33:50,195
Yeah?

367
00:33:51,279 --> 00:33:52,530
You wanted me, sir?

368
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:55,742
Well, you've been gone a lot.

369
00:33:56,701 --> 00:33:58,036
Come take a seat.

370
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:11,757
These are records of Ikeda Yuji

371
00:34:11,758 --> 00:34:14,009
laundering Cheon's slush funds in Japan.

372
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:15,011
Take a look.

373
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:23,353
So where were you today anyway?

374
00:34:25,855 --> 00:34:27,691
Baek Soyeong met me for coffee.

375
00:34:28,566 --> 00:34:30,360
Okay, why did you meet with her, then?

376
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:35,990
Because of a dealer named Park Changbae
who works for her.

377
00:34:35,991 --> 00:34:39,536
He was pushing meth in Busan,
but he suddenly vanished, so…

378
00:34:40,370 --> 00:34:42,121
I met with her briefly. Big deal.

379
00:34:42,122 --> 00:34:44,040
I told you to hold off for now.

380
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,879
I'm not gonna do that, sir.

381
00:34:51,172 --> 00:34:53,717
Want me to just send you back
to Busan, Yejin?

382
00:34:56,928 --> 00:34:59,306
The reason I'm here
is to bust drug dealers.

383
00:35:01,474 --> 00:35:04,101
I honestly don't give a damn
about the slush fund.

384
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:07,938
A drug dealer should go down for drugs.
And that includes Baek Kitae.

385
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:10,190
He belongs in prison,
and until I catch the guy,

386
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:11,609
I'm not going back, all right?

387
00:35:11,610 --> 00:35:13,652
The money he brought in
from his meth empire

388
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:15,154
is in the slush fund!

389
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:18,907
Then answer me. Why?
Why drop the drug charges?

390
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:23,663
What about this don't you get?

391
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:27,375
You listen to me.

392
00:35:29,002 --> 00:35:32,130
You've really been confusing
the shit out of me lately.

393
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:35,800
Are you actually trying to
bring down a drug lord,

394
00:35:36,301 --> 00:35:40,221
or are you just backing military trash
so you can take power later on?

395
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,016
So tell me…

396
00:35:45,393 --> 00:35:47,646
what exactly is your real objective here?

397
00:36:38,738 --> 00:36:40,824
Minju. Minju? Hey, Minju.

398
00:36:42,075 --> 00:36:43,243
Are you all right?

399
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:45,578
- Uncle Kihyun.
- Mm-hmm?

400
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:53,669
Ah, shit.

401
00:36:59,801 --> 00:37:02,261
Soyeong. Soyeong. Hey.

402
00:37:04,139 --> 00:37:07,141
Soyeong. Hey, what's wrong? Huh?

403
00:37:07,142 --> 00:37:08,226
What is it?

404
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:13,564
Hey!

405
00:37:23,283 --> 00:37:26,034
- Get away!
- Soyeong! Soyeong!

406
00:37:29,414 --> 00:37:31,457
Get away from me!

407
00:37:31,458 --> 00:37:34,793
No, no! Get away!

408
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:36,295
It's me! Soyeong!

409
00:37:36,296 --> 00:37:39,299
Hey! It's me, Kihyun. It's Kihyun.

410
00:37:40,175 --> 00:37:41,926
Yeah.

411
00:37:45,847 --> 00:37:47,222
It's me. It's me.

412
00:37:55,982 --> 00:37:57,609
Da… Daeil.

413
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:05,240
I'm sorry.

414
00:38:08,745 --> 00:38:10,288
I'm so sorry.

415
00:38:11,247 --> 00:38:12,373
I'm sorry.

416
00:38:15,126 --> 00:38:16,877
I'm sorry.

417
00:38:21,508 --> 00:38:23,550
I'm sorry.

418
00:38:23,551 --> 00:38:24,719
You're all right, hey.

419
00:38:25,512 --> 00:38:26,804
It's okay.

420
00:38:26,805 --> 00:38:29,348
- It's okay.
- I'm so sorry.

421
00:38:35,188 --> 00:38:37,481
- Minju…
- Hey, Minju's all right. Minju's fine.

422
00:38:37,482 --> 00:38:39,274
- Minju.
- She's fine, okay?

423
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:40,400
Minju.

424
00:38:40,401 --> 00:38:43,196
Minju. Dad's here! Don't be scared!

425
00:38:43,905 --> 00:38:45,364
- Minju, Dad's here!
-  Hey, no…

426
00:38:45,365 --> 00:38:46,824
- No, stop, Soyeong.
- Hey, Minju!

427
00:38:46,825 --> 00:38:48,534
- Minju!
- That's enough.

428
00:38:48,535 --> 00:38:50,410
- Soyeong, no!
- Minju!

429
00:38:50,411 --> 00:38:53,164
Minju!

430
00:39:05,385 --> 00:39:08,512
HANGUK UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

431
00:39:44,716 --> 00:39:46,926
Did you know Soyeong was like this?

432
00:39:47,677 --> 00:39:48,887
That it was this bad?

433
00:39:54,434 --> 00:39:56,519
If I had, I wouldn't have left her alone.

434
00:39:59,355 --> 00:40:01,273
She'll be fine once she gets treatment.

435
00:40:01,274 --> 00:40:03,276
I'm going to do
everything I can to help her.

436
00:40:05,904 --> 00:40:07,655
Are you capable of regret?

437
00:40:09,991 --> 00:40:10,992
What?

438
00:40:11,951 --> 00:40:13,286
Do you ever regret…

439
00:40:15,163 --> 00:40:16,747
the way you've lived your life?

440
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:33,806
What the hell did you just say?

441
00:40:34,641 --> 00:40:37,435
Who do you think put food on your table
all these years?

442
00:40:38,478 --> 00:40:41,105
I was the one earning the money
that fed and clothed you.

443
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:45,693
I put you through the Military Academy.

444
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:48,779
You've kept your mouth shut all this time,

445
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:50,990
and suddenly you've got
a pang of conscience?

446
00:40:51,532 --> 00:40:52,866
And did you notice?

447
00:40:52,867 --> 00:40:56,371
You didn't even realize
what was going on with your own sister!

448
00:40:57,455 --> 00:40:59,331
Just carry on and forget it!

449
00:40:59,332 --> 00:41:01,124
While I take care of everything!

450
00:41:01,125 --> 00:41:02,502
Don't say that!

451
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:07,881
You have got to stop pretending
to be responsible for everything.

452
00:41:07,882 --> 00:41:10,008
Soyeong and I always listened to you.

453
00:41:10,009 --> 00:41:12,345
We spent our whole lives
doing your bidding.

454
00:41:13,972 --> 00:41:16,473
If I had known you were gonna
end up like this,

455
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:18,726
I would never have lived that way.

456
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:23,356
Sure, you built a drug ring just for us.

457
00:41:25,775 --> 00:41:28,611
Not cause of your bottomless,
all-consuming ambition.

458
00:41:45,837 --> 00:41:47,504
How dare you, you little shit.

459
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:13,990
This is exactly what you did back then.

460
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:17,910
You never asked about the gun I stole…

461
00:42:20,830 --> 00:42:23,082
or why I shot him in the first place.

462
00:42:24,625 --> 00:42:27,295
Whether it was right or wrong.

463
00:42:30,173 --> 00:42:32,592
You never once said
a single word about it.

464
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:37,596
Everything went bad from then on.

465
00:42:50,777 --> 00:42:53,361
If you were really that unhappy
about me saving your life,

466
00:42:53,362 --> 00:42:54,697
you could've said so.

467
00:42:55,281 --> 00:42:57,283
From now on, live how you want.

468
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:25,937
Chief Cheon, I hope you slept a little.

469
00:43:28,189 --> 00:43:29,941
It's not a five-course dinner,

470
00:43:30,608 --> 00:43:32,734
but I thought I'd bring you
something to eat.

471
00:43:32,735 --> 00:43:33,736
Here.

472
00:43:34,946 --> 00:43:37,115
You should have a little soju too.

473
00:44:11,149 --> 00:44:14,152
CHIEF OF STAFF TO THE PRESIDENT
CHEON'S SLUSH FUND SCANDAL

474
00:44:17,029 --> 00:44:18,156
So, that money.

475
00:44:19,574 --> 00:44:21,658
What were you planning to do with it?

476
00:44:21,659 --> 00:44:24,829
And it was all from drugs, right?
All 70 billion?

477
00:44:26,038 --> 00:44:29,500
Looks like you were planning to use it
to make yourself president.

478
00:44:30,126 --> 00:44:31,127
Wait a second.

479
00:44:32,128 --> 00:44:34,129
If you'd been able to pull that off,

480
00:44:34,130 --> 00:44:37,132
meth would've become
our biggest national industry.

481
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:45,057
It was Baek Kitae's idea though, right?

482
00:44:51,105 --> 00:44:54,901
Man, you're really desperate
to catch Baek Kitae, aren't you?

483
00:44:58,821 --> 00:45:00,948
You must still be holding a grudge…

484
00:45:02,742 --> 00:45:05,244
over what he did to you.

485
00:45:06,871 --> 00:45:08,289
Come on, you and Kitae?

486
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:13,211
When it really comes down to it,
you guys are two of a kind,

487
00:45:14,378 --> 00:45:15,379
yeah?

488
00:45:33,105 --> 00:45:34,315
Hmm.

489
00:45:37,818 --> 00:45:39,779
Seems like talking's unproductive.

490
00:45:44,575 --> 00:45:47,161
- What, am I gonna be tortured next?
- Torture?

491
00:45:48,162 --> 00:45:49,747
That's always been your specialty.

492
00:45:50,289 --> 00:45:52,374
Ya know, waterboarding and all that?

493
00:45:52,375 --> 00:45:55,086
Killed plenty of guys like that
back in the day, didn't you?

494
00:45:56,128 --> 00:45:59,090
All the techniques you used
back then are still around.

495
00:46:00,258 --> 00:46:03,427
Your methods are being carried on
by the next generation.

496
00:46:06,806 --> 00:46:08,431
We're ready.

497
00:46:11,936 --> 00:46:13,271
Clothes off.

498
00:46:42,133 --> 00:46:45,636
I think the madam here
knows Hwang Daesik pretty well by now.

499
00:46:46,137 --> 00:46:48,847
Whenever he plans to meet someone
discreetly, this is where he brings them.

500
00:46:48,848 --> 00:46:49,849
HEAVEN CLOUD PAVILION

501
00:46:52,810 --> 00:46:55,020
From what I've gathered,
he goes there regularly,

502
00:46:55,021 --> 00:46:56,354
at least once a month.

503
00:46:56,355 --> 00:46:59,650
He usually arrives in the evening
and stays for around three hours.

504
00:47:00,276 --> 00:47:03,194
This house is about a hundred meters
from Heaven Cloud Pavilion,

505
00:47:03,195 --> 00:47:05,489
so we'll be using it
as our base of operations.

506
00:47:06,240 --> 00:47:09,452
The owner and his family
have already been sent out of town.

507
00:47:15,041 --> 00:47:16,207
This is C-4.

508
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:18,711
They used it for breaching
and demolition during the Vietnam War.

509
00:47:21,339 --> 00:47:23,174
It has a lethal radius of 50 meters,

510
00:47:23,966 --> 00:47:26,926
and about the same explosive power
as six hand grenades.

511
00:47:26,927 --> 00:47:29,305
As you can see, it's fitted with a timer.

512
00:47:30,139 --> 00:47:33,184
Once we activate the detonator
remotely from the operations base,

513
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:36,604
it'll start counting down.

514
00:47:37,229 --> 00:47:40,398
Now, if you cut this red wire,
the countdown will stop.

515
00:47:40,399 --> 00:47:42,192
It has to be the red wire.

516
00:47:42,193 --> 00:47:45,237
If you cut the blue one by mistake,
it'll go off immediately.

517
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:48,824
All the pieces are in place.

518
00:47:50,159 --> 00:47:51,160
Director.

519
00:47:53,037 --> 00:47:54,205
Shall we do this?

520
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:49,468
Start it.

521
00:48:59,812 --> 00:49:03,773
Uh, I know that everyone's been busy
serving the country,

522
00:49:03,774 --> 00:49:05,651
so I appreciate you making the time.

523
00:49:06,277 --> 00:49:08,862
In return, I can promise you one thing…

524
00:49:08,863 --> 00:49:11,990
'cause you're my friends,
you're gonna be treated right today!

525
00:49:14,660 --> 00:49:16,911
All right, with that in mind…

526
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:20,958
Raise a glass.

527
00:49:23,544 --> 00:49:25,880
- We are…
-  We are one!

528
00:49:30,509 --> 00:49:33,554
Huh?

529
00:49:54,617 --> 00:49:57,660
I didn't gather you all here
just for fun today.

530
00:49:57,661 --> 00:50:02,124
I also wanted to introduce you
to the newest JIH member.

531
00:50:04,335 --> 00:50:07,129
This man is, well, how should I put this…

532
00:50:07,755 --> 00:50:11,634
He's the brains
behind our latest operation.

533
00:50:12,384 --> 00:50:14,219
Our very own Zhuge Liang.

534
00:50:14,220 --> 00:50:17,431
Let's welcome our advisor, Jang Geonyoung.

535
00:50:28,067 --> 00:50:29,318
Nice to meet everybody.

536
00:50:30,236 --> 00:50:32,570
Given the rise of instability and crime,

537
00:50:32,571 --> 00:50:36,324
I plan to do my absolute best
for the Joint Investigation Headquarters,

538
00:50:36,325 --> 00:50:39,410
rooting out corruption,
abuses of government power,

539
00:50:39,411 --> 00:50:41,497
and money laundering
taking place overseas.

540
00:50:42,456 --> 00:50:43,791
I appreciate your support.

541
00:50:44,291 --> 00:50:45,292
Let's hear it for him.

542
00:50:51,882 --> 00:50:53,425
Wait a minute, isn't that…

543
00:50:54,426 --> 00:50:55,427
Director.

544
00:50:57,221 --> 00:50:58,514
Isn't that your brother?

545
00:50:59,306 --> 00:51:00,307
What did you say?

546
00:51:40,472 --> 00:51:41,849
Sir!

547
00:51:43,559 --> 00:51:46,312
I got into a minor accident on my way.
Sorry I'm late.

548
00:51:46,895 --> 00:51:49,564
Oh, no. You're not hurt, are you?

549
00:51:49,565 --> 00:51:50,982
No, sir. I'm fine.

550
00:51:50,983 --> 00:51:53,401
I see you've got good looks
and spirit, too.

551
00:51:53,402 --> 00:51:54,485
Tell me your name?

552
00:51:54,486 --> 00:51:56,446
Lieutenant Colonel Baek Kihyun, sir!

553
00:51:56,447 --> 00:51:58,990
All right. Happy to have you here.

554
00:51:58,991 --> 00:52:00,074
Much appreciated.

555
00:52:00,075 --> 00:52:02,869
Colonel Baek, take a seat down there.

556
00:52:02,870 --> 00:52:03,871
Yes, of course.

557
00:52:07,124 --> 00:52:08,125
Thank you.

558
00:52:31,065 --> 00:52:33,983
This time, how about
we let Colonel Baek take the lead.

559
00:52:33,984 --> 00:52:36,320
Just give us a nice, proud "We are."

560
00:52:37,196 --> 00:52:38,197
We are!

561
00:52:38,822 --> 00:52:39,990
We are one!

562
00:52:52,002 --> 00:52:54,797
-  What's this?
- Hey, not yet. What's going on?

563
00:52:55,381 --> 00:52:57,256
I don't believe I called for you.

564
00:52:57,257 --> 00:53:00,843
Well, General,
I couldn't help myself.

565
00:53:00,844 --> 00:53:02,513
I called for them, sir.
